    "_comment": [
      "Sampling, not greedy. pass^k asks whether a model succeeds on all k",
      "independent attempts, which is only a question if the attempts can",
      "differ. At temperature 0 every run is identical and pass^k collapses",
      "to pass^1, measuring nothing the blueprint is about.",
      "One setting is used for every model. Publishers recommend different",
      "values per family, so adopting any one family's recommendation would",
      "hand that family an advantage the comparison is supposed to measure.",
      "See D-067."
    ]
